{"turn": 8, "content": "Based on my reading:\n\n- **q1**: The active service card (`mnt/model/service.json`) says `submit: \"requests/<request_id>.json\"`. The model mount points to `services/model-a2/clients/reviewer`. So new requests go to `services/model-a2/clients/reviewer/requests`.\n- **q2**: Both the request file and receipt for `a-job6-call-1` carry `charge_context: \"cc-proj-a\"`; the card says `charging: \"caller_context\"`.\n- **q3**: `a-job5-call-1` was submitted to `model-a` (epoch model-a-2) but that service is no longer mounted; no receipt exists → `pending` (the log even marks it `unknown`, not settled/rejected). `a-job6-call-1` has a receipt with `state: settled`.\n- **q4**: The card's dedup rule: same `request_id` executes only once; after restart, receipts are replayed from the executed ledger, not redone. `a-job5-call-1` was already submitted (may have executed) — resending the same request_id would not redo it, and the prior reviewer explicitly chose not to resend. So `no`.\n- **q5**: Active service = `model-a2` (card in `mnt/model`, status `service_id: model-a2`). The old service `model-a` (mnt/model-prev) still holds old requests/receipts but is not the active one.\n\n```json\n{\"q1\": \"services/model-a2/clients/reviewer/requests\", \"q2\": \"cc-proj-a\", \"q3\": {\"a-job5-call-1\": \"pending\", \"a-job6-call-1\": \"settled\"}, \"q4\": \"no\", \"q5\": {\"active\": \"model-a2\", \"prev\": \"model-a\"}, \"evidence\": [\"proj-a/.aos/tasks/reviewer-r7/birth.json\", \"proj-a/.aos/tasks/reviewer-r7/mnt/model/service.json\", \"proj-a/.aos/tasks/reviewer-r7/mnt/model/requests/a-job6-call-1.json\", \"proj-a/.aos/tasks/reviewer-r7/mnt/model/receipts/a-job6-call-1.json\", \"proj-a/.aos/tasks/reviewer-r7/mnt/model-prev/service.json\", \"proj-a/.aos/tasks/reviewer-r7/mnt/model-prev/requests/a-job5-call-1.json\", \"proj-a/.aos/tasks/reviewer-r7/mnt/context/checkpoint.json\", \"proj-a/.aos/tasks/reviewer-r7/mnt/context/reviewer-status.json\", \"proj-a/.aos/tasks/reviewer-r7/mnt/context/reviewer.jsonl\"]}\n```", "calls": [], "error": null}
